{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner read the complete 519-line N4 revision 2 at c938f0cb1d90ef32491b37c04ec72fede9819d63 in two complete spans, and verified the branch ref. It incorporates the five proposed defaults and A–H maps, restores all four original situations in the arranged cold scenario, retains exact intent and separate owners, and removes the mandatory second full cold run. This is a planning observation, not independent guarded review or adoption.\n\nTargeted further source reads at d691 covered actual MCP read/land runners and schemas, client HTTPS/RPC error wrapping, R-CRED-10, R-IDEM-2 and R-DECL-10. Six narrow corrections remain. The first corrects my own 87440e direction; the others qualify the revision's source-derived promises.\n\n1. I was wrong to offer an own-reservation explanation under the reserved refusal. R-DECL-10 says the designated member's take ends the reservation, while anyone else is refused reserved. Therefore a caller actually refused by that platform rule is not the designated member. Section 4.2 should name that fact, point to the recorded reservation/deadline and eventual reservation-ended event, and allow waiting or other deliberately authorized work. Do not tell that refused caller it may simply take as the named member. This changes none of the reviewed reservation contract.\n\n2. Section 3 currently puts land with waitMs in the read/wait row and says nothing was written by this call. Actual MCP land is a write followed by an optional wait: run.ts first calls room.land, then waits on the returned landing.op. Keep its accepted/refused/unknown admission separate from its operation wait. MCP operation and attention are read/waits; their bounded expiry returns current state/an empty page, while RoomApi.wait itself throws timeout and the MCP wrappers catch it. A transport failure is another case. Do not generalize those different boundaries into every wait returning state. State the actual missing-read shapes too: MCP explain returns {act, outcome:\"not-found\"}, lane/proposal/operation include what, acts has outcome only; RoomApi lane/proposal/explain/actsAt can return null, while op can throw not-found. No new shape or API is needed.\n\n3. Without maybeRecorded is not, alone, proof that a write was not recorded across every transport. The HTTPS source supplies the flag on lost POST responses and trusts an actual Room ArtroomError's admission semantics, but RPC guard can turn an otherwise unclassified thrown error into internal without that field. This source read does not reproduce a lost result or commission a core defect/fix. The design should use a known pre-send failure or a trusted explicit Room admission answer for definite non-recording; a delivered write with no reliable outcome remains uncertain even when its transport omitted the flag. Honor retryable and retryAfterMs without treating them as a recording verdict. Where no reliable phase/receipt is available, retain original intent and show uncertainty, rather than invent certainty from an absent optional field.\n\n4. Section 6's lost/revoked-credential statement must distinguish bearer sessions from retained signed envelopes. R-CRED-10 rejects even a historical bearer retry after its session ended; there is no envelope for that session to replay. It explicitly distinguishes someone who kept a signed envelope. Under R-IDEM-2 the exact signed bytes of an accepted act return the original record even after the signing key was revoked; a private signer is not needed to re-sign those saved bytes. An act not previously accepted is still judged at admission and can be refused under current authority. Keep that supported reconciliation; do not claim every lost key or revoked credential makes an already signed original impossible to submit, or authorize a new credential/intent as a substitute. Private task-read and broker/device authority remain their own boundaries. The general wording in 87440e about credentials was expressly for bearer MCP and must not be broadened to erase the signed-envelope case.\n\n5. In section 4.1, a currently active policy snapshot is not automatically the policy that governed an earlier refused act. Classification must use the relevant retained version/recorded evidence, with activation races and completeness stated. Nor does absence of a matching decision in an incomplete or unsupported trace prove platform origin. If the available data cannot establish the source at that outcome, keep unclassified and the Room's words. This adds no new discriminator, read or test gate.\n\n6. The cold scenario should leave its absent summarize path as authoritative discovery plus qualified reporting. A delegated caller with no grant for an undeclared kind can fail authority first under R-ADM's order; do not promise kind-undeclared if it tries anyway. The changed-answer case deliberately keeps the old binding in the old grant, then reaches binding-stale as described; preserve that actual arrangement. Also the text says the run adds one observation of revocation, but no revocation is arranged. Remove that unsupported planned witness rather than add another revocation case. Reuse the already reviewed revocation evidence with its actual scope, as the original request requires; retain the agent's arranged lost-result recovery and all four situation/changed-meaning/operation witnesses. The question desk code hold must use its actual active conflict policy when arranging scope-overlap, not merely an unverified global exclusive label.\n\nNo further implementation or runtime test follows from these corrections. Preserve complete original N4, the client/MCP/Stage5 and C1–C6/N3/N5/N6 owners, exact independent design review/adoption before separate implementation, the highest test-overhead priority and builder's Jam readiness judgment. No source approval, original closure or first-Jam gate is supplied.","body":{"head":"c938f0cb1d90ef32491b37c04ec72fede9819d63","no_git_artifact":"true","scope":"Complete revision-2 planning read, correct planner reservation wording and remaining recovery/read qualifications; no runtime commission","source_approval":"none"}}